n("n942","s061-01","vtrum persona secundum quod dicit aliquid commune patri filio et spiritui sancto dicat precipue aliquid secunde intentionis","la","source","Corresponds to Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 23 q. un. (whether ‘person’, as common to the three, signifies a second intention).","to-verify")
n("n943","s061-02","opinio Egidii","la","source","Giles of Rome, *In I Sent.* d. 23.","to-verify")
n("n944","s061-02","intentio Varronis libro. 1.","la","intertext","William of Ware (*Varro*; see n895, n923), *In I Sent.* d. 23. This is the third named citation of Ware in pp. 91–97.","to-verify")
n("n945","s061-03","persona est intellectualis nature indiuidua subsistentia","la","intertext","This conflates Boethius, *Contra Eutychen* 3 (*naturae rationabilis individua substantia*), with Richard of St Victor, *De Trin.* IV 22 (*intellectualis naturae incommunicabilis existentia*). Gorris attributes the hybrid to Richard.","verified")
n("n946","s061-03","persona est obiectum fruitionis","la","doctrinal","The persons are the object of *fruitio* (Augustine, *De doctr. christ.* I 5.5: *res quibus fruendum est, Pater et Filius et Spiritus sanctus*).","verified")
n("n947","s061-04","quando actualiter intelligeret","la","textual","Section breaks off at the end of p. 97, the last page of the first PDF. The text continues in the next part.","certain")

