n("n1122","s061-04","Sed Franciscus","la","historical","Probably Francis of Meyronnes OFM († c. 1328), whom Gorris uses elsewhere; a marginal hand in A seems to read *…maron*. Locus in Meyronnes (*Conflatus* I d. 23) not checked.","probable")
n("n1123","s061-04","in esse quidditatiuo","la","textual","A prints *inesse quidditatiuo*; divided as *in esse* (cf. *esse quidditatiuum* above). Reading *inesse* (‘to belong’) is grammatically possible but gives a weaker sense.","probable")
n("n1124","s061-04","Tertia conclusio quod quidditas","la","textual","Running headline of p. 98 reads *Di.xxiiii. Q.ii*, although the page contains the end of d. 23 and d. 24 has a single question; the headline is anomalous.","certain")
n("n1125","s061-04","persona. suppositum. singulare et indiuiduum","la","commentary","The fourfold order of decreasing extension (person ⊂ *suppositum* ⊂ singular ⊂ individual, with ass, stone and whiteness as examples) is a school commonplace; its immediate source has not been identified.","to-verify")
n("n1126","s061-05","rationes distinctas","la","textual","A has no final punctuation mark.","certain")
